<title>INDIA: India's MTNL 1st half 96/97 net rises.</title>
<headline>India's MTNL 1st half 96/97 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to end-September</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		 4,362.4  vs   3,222.9</p>
<p>    Income from services  19,622.5  vs  17,954.8</p>
<p>    Other income		 210.7  vs     155.0</p>
<p>    Total Expenditure	9,488.1  vs   8,683.6</p>
<p>    Interest		     800.3  vs     920.0</p>
<p>    Depreciation	     2,460.2  vs   2,559.8</p>
<p>    Tax provision	    2,722.2  vs   2,723.5</p>
<p>NOTE: Indian state-owned Mahanagar Nigam Telephone Ltd (MTNL) said in a statement that network utilisation charges and licence fees were under discussion with the Department of Telecommunications, &quot;as a result of which certain changes may take place in the above figures&quot;. It did not elaborate.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
